    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d952">

                <pb facs="0887" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/16670: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-09T20:00:00-04:00">June 9, 1941—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>318. Chungking’s 224, June 6, noon. The Department assumes that you will
                    supplement your recent representations (your 771, June 5, 9 p.m.<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d952-f1"/>) with a further emphatic protest against this endangering
                    of personnel and premises of the American Embassy. You may wish to point out
                    that any further recurrence will not comport with the assurances of the War
                        Minister<anchor n="36" xml:id="d952-f2"/> mentioned by Mr. Matsuoka in your
                    781, June 6, 8 p.m.<anchor n="37" xml:id="d952-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Shanghai. Repeated to Chungking, Peiping, Hankow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d952-f1" n="35" xml:id="d952-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see Ambassador Grew’s despatch No. 5645, June 10, together with
                    enclosures, <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_713">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, pp. 713</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_715">715</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d952-f2" n="36" xml:id="d952-f2-content">
